# PID Tuning Guide

## Altitude PID

Increase Kp:
- Faster takeoff
- Too high = oscillation

Increase Ki:
- Removes steady-state altitude error

Increase Kd:
- Reduces bounce / overshoot

---

## Drift PID (X,Y)

Increase Kp:
- Faster drift correction

Too high:
- Aggressive twitching

Kd:
- Smooth movement

---

## Recommended Start Values

Altitude:
Kp = 0.4
Ki = 0.02
Kd = 0.25

XY:
Kp = 0.3
Ki = 0.01
Kd = 0.15